\section*{AP \({ }^{\text {® }}\) CALCULUS BC \\ 2007 SCORING GUIDELINES (Form B)}

\section*{Question 2}

An object moving along a curve in the \(x y\)-plane is at position \((x(t), y(t))\) at time \(t\) with
\[
\frac{d x}{d t}=\arctan \left(\frac{t}{1+t}\right) \text { and } \frac{d y}{d t}=\ln \left(t^{2}+1\right)
\]
for \(t \geq 0\). At time \(t=0\), the object is at position ( \(-3,-4\) ). (Note: \(\tan ^{-1} x=\arctan x\) )
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] Find the speed of the object at time \(t=4\).
\item[(b)] Find the total distance traveled by the object over the time interval \(0 \leq t \leq 4\).
\item[(c)] Find \(x(4)\).
\item[(d)] For \(t>0\), there is a point on the curve where the line tangent to the curve has slope 2 . At what time \(t\) is the object at this point? Find the acceleration vector at this point.
\item[(a)] Speed \(=\sqrt{x^{\prime}(4)^{2}+y^{\prime}(4)^{2}}=2.912\)
\item[(b)] Distance \(=\int_{0}^{4} \sqrt{\left(\frac{d x}{d t}\right)^{2}+\left(\frac{d y}{d t}\right)^{2}} d t=6.423\)
\item[(c)]
\[
\begin{aligned}
x(4) & =x(0)+\int_{0}^{4} x^{\prime}(t) d t \\
& =-3+2.10794=-0.892
\end{aligned}
\]
\item[(d)] The slope is 2, so \(\frac{\frac{d y}{d t}}{\frac{d x}{d t}}=2\), or \(\ln \left(t^{2}+1\right)=2 \arctan \left(\frac{t}{1+t}\right)\).
Since \(t>0, t=1.35766\). At this time, the acceleration is \(\left.\left\langle x^{\prime \prime}(t), y^{\prime \prime}(t)\right\rangle\right|_{t=1.35766}=\langle 0.135,0.955\rangle\).
\end{itemize}

1 : speed at \(t=4\)
\(2:\left\{\begin{array}{l}1: \text { integral } \\ 1: \text { answer }\end{array}\right.\)
\begin{itemize}
\item[] \(3:\left\{\begin{array}{l}2:\left\{\begin{array}{l}1: \text { integrand } \\ 1: \text { uses } x(0)=-3\end{array}\right. \\ 1: \text { answer }\end{array}\right.\)
\(3:\left\{\begin{array}{l}1: \frac{\frac{d y}{d t}}{\frac{d x}{d t}}=2 \\ 1: t \text {-value } \\ 1: \text { values for } x^{\prime \prime} \text { and } y^{\prime \prime}\end{array}\right.\)
\end{itemize}
